# DIAR-SMOKE read attempt 2 — identical harness crash, root cause isolated to the slicer
# 2026-08-19, HEAD ec829d42f83782aebe17cfac1442bf4228107ba7 (clean tree; audio-derived slicer
# inputs wired per attempt 1's diagnosis), WSL Ubuntu-24.04, ~/.venvs/speechrl,
# PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1. Same command as attempt 1. Exit code: 1. No verdict.json /
# report.txt written; no DER/JER/packing number produced or observed.
#
# The violation reproduced byte-identically (slice 22, start=2035.2585, end=2160.5665,
# 125.308 s > 120.0 s) at scripts/diar_smoke_read.py:166 -> diar_smoke_scoring.py:229
# (packing_change_for_meeting, ORACLE plan) because the attempt-1 diagnosis was incomplete
# on two counts, established by scratchpad-only structural diagnostics (turn-boundary times
# and group bounds only; no transcript content, no tool-side exposure):
#
# 1. The crashing meeting is TS3004d (registered meeting six of six — ES2011a, ES2011b,
#    IS1008b, IS1008d, and TS3004b all scored without error in both attempts), not TS3004b
#    as attempt 1's log first recorded. TS3004b's oracle plan builds cleanly at HEAD
#    (24 slices, no near-cap slice), with or without audio-derived inputs.
# 2. Audio-derived pause transitions cannot rescue TS3004d: detect_energy_pause_transitions
#    finds ZERO transitions on the whole 2750.8 s meeting (dense speech; TS3004b has 38).
#    The real root cause is in meeting_minutes_agent/chunking/slicer.py itself: interior
#    gap-midpoint tiling in build_turn_aware_slice_plan added a FLAT half-gap to each
#    neighboring slice with no room cap. TS3004d's oracle turn table carries turn group
#    [2035.272, 2136.408] (101.136 s, 23 turns) followed by a 48.317 s inter-group silence
#    gap; midpoint tiling added 24.1585 s and 0.0135 s halves -> 125.308 s > 120.0 s.
#    This is the same bug class commit e627f8e fixed for EDGE slices (room-capped snap
#    margins); the interior case was latent because no prior consumer ever built a full
#    turn-aware plan for TS3004d (the P-ATTR manifest's four meetings exclude it; its
#    committed full plans carry no oversized slice).
#
# Resolution (committed immediately after this record, before the one-shot read execution):
# room-capped interior gap tiling in build_turn_aware_slice_plan — each neighbor absorbs at
# most its remaining room under max_s, leftover spills to the other side's room, residual
# silence stays uncovered rather than oversizing a slice. Behavior-preserving for every
# previously-valid plan: when both rooms cover their half-gaps the split is the plain
# midpoint (regression-guarded by test_interior_gap_tiling_still_splits_at_the_midpoint_
# when_room_allows; the TS3004d geometry is regression-guarded by
# test_a_wide_interior_silence_gap_does_not_push_a_slice_past_max_s).
# The flown run directory was not touched in either attempt.
